From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:42:01 -0500
Subject: fix: pass another Space's tab in the pinned run

Every Space's tabs share the one strip, and a loose tab of Home can sit between
Work's pins: Home's pin put in a split with one of Home's tabs brings that tab up
to it, a split stays where it is, and the tab stays there when the split ends.
Each walk along the run stopped at the first tab that was no pin, whichever
Space it was in. In Work a new pin landed before Work's last pin, out of the
order pinned, and could land in the middle of Home's split, which broke it. An
unpin, and a link opened from a pin, stayed above Work's last pin, so that pin
was drawn under the Clear line. A pinned folder went to the top of the run.

The walks now go by the rows of the tab's own Space: another Space's loose tab
does not end the run, and the end is never inside a split or a folder that has a
loose tab, because that row ended the run before it.

Why: pins H14 (BACKLOG S-314). The pin, the unpin, the link and the folder were
each seen wrong through the model and the sidebar's rows.
Removable when: the Space model and its pinned run leave the series.
